# C++ style

Follow the Header / Source / Brace / Variable declarations sections in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

Reminders:

- `.hpp` for headers, `.cpp` for sources; definitions in headers, implementations in sources
- Header order: guards → includes → macros → types → free functions → classes → justified namespaces
- Do not wrap a lone free function or class in a named namespace; namespaces need a real multi-symbol/collision purpose (see `AGENTS.md`)
- Helpers (one-site / file-local) must live in an anonymous namespace; actual/reusable functions need abstract params or a repeating pattern — do not promote helpers to headers on speculation (see `AGENTS.md`)
- No passthrough wrappers: same parameter count/types forwarded unchanged is just a rename; wrappers must process or derive arguments (see `AGENTS.md`)
- Declare variables at the start of their scope (prefer function scope; branch/loop OK if local-only); blank line after the declaration block (see `AGENTS.md`)
- Every `#endif` needs a condition comment
- Same-line `{` for namespace/class/function; next-line `{` for conditions/loops
- Do not `using` a namespace you are implementing; avoid globals unless the user asks
